'''Nicola's''' was a small beverage shop located outside [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva Andor's]] [[Andor household|family residence]].<ref name="Daughter of Ferrix">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}}</ref> The name of the business was written in [[Bazeese script]] and was printed in [[Color|blue]] letters at the top of the building, with red lettering going around the window saying "NICOLA'S [[Tea|TEAROOMS]] REFRESHMENTS HERE [[Caf|CAFF]] <small>''[sic]''</small> SERVED".<ref name="Daughter of Ferrix">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}}</ref><ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|AurekFonts|status/1592990145481179137|AurekFonts|date=2022-11-16|quote=____ TEAROOMS REFRESHMENTS HERE CAFF SERVED|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/8cFEG}}<br />{{Twitter|BazatronPrime|status/1593168767659671552|[[Barry Gingell]]|date=2022-11-17|quote=I believe the missing word is Nicola's :D|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/gNnuQ}}</ref>

When searching for Maarva's son [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian]], [[Vel Sartha]] observed the home and two of Andor's friends, [[Bix Caleen]] and [[Brasso]], from Nicola's across the street; while waiting for her lover, [[Cinta Kaz]], to join her. Sartha's drink went [[Temperature|cold]] in the meantime.<ref name="Narkina">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref> Kaz remained on Ferrix afterward and blended in among the locals, taking a job at Nicola's in the [[Standard week|week]] before Maarva Andor [[Death|died]]. An [[ISB Attendant|attendant]] for the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] (ISB), [[Corv]], also pretended to be a civilian, which Kaz noticed.<ref name="One Way Out">{{Andor|One Way Out}}</ref> Aware that he was ISB, she kept a close eye on him when he visited Nicola's, which they both used to observe the Andor home.<ref name="Daughter of Ferrix">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}}</ref>

